Common Garage Door Problems
Many homeowners experience similar garage door issues. Recognising these warning signs early can help prevent major repairs.
Broken Garage Door Springs
Garage door springs carry the weight of the door and allow it to open and close smoothly. A broken spring can make the door difficult or impossible to lift safely.
Worn Rollers and Tracks
Damaged rollers or bent tracks often cause noisy operation and uneven movement. Replacing worn components restores smooth performance.
Garage Door Opener Issues
If your garage door opener stops responding, opens inconsistently, or reverses unexpectedly, professional troubleshooting can identify electrical or mechanical problems.
Damaged Cables
Garage door cables work alongside the springs to lift the door safely. Frayed or snapped cables should always be replaced by trained technicians.
Misaligned Sensors
Modern garage doors include safety sensors that prevent accidents. Dirty or misaligned sensors may stop the door from closing properly.

